The abstract describes a legal QA system that combines keyword extraction, dispute categorisation, and legal knowledge retrieval. It is evaluated on three datasets against baselines that include LegalBERT+RAG. This suggests a retrieval-conditioned generation system with experiments.

"Multi-modal" here probably refers to a reasoning framework over text, since the datasets are text corpora, so E9 (multimodal-only RAG) does not clearly apply. Whether the generator actually conditions on retrieved text is somewhat uncertain, but the mention of retrieval, generation and a RAG baseline leans toward inclusion.

